			  speed. However, the height should be sufficient to avoid contamination on the ground" (a380_fcom.txt
			  l.151175-151176): a jettison on the ground puts the fuel on the ground. The FQMS (FuelJettison.ts) does not
			  inhibit it on the ground (JETTISON ARM + ACTIVE pb-sw on the overhead FUEL panel).
			- Same per-side condition as the plume (L:A380X_FUEL_JETTISON_IN_PROGRESS and that side's jettison valve 57 / 58
			  open), and SIM ON GROUND. Like the plume, not tied to the flyPad Settings > Sim Options switch "Situation
			  Visual Effects" (user decision 2026-10-12: the jettison effect is not a situation effect, plume and drip
			  always show together).
